Interview-Friendly Answer (30 sec)

Best practices for JWT include using short-lived access tokens with refresh tokens,
storing tokens securely (HTTP-only cookies), always validating signature and expiration,
using strong signing algorithms, avoiding sensitive data in the payload, and transmitting tokens only over HTTPS.
These practices ensure secure and scalable stateless authentication.

